      <span class="search-hit">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2506.23862v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        We introduce context augmentation, a data-augmentation approach that uses large <span class="search-hit mathjax">language</span> <span class="search-hit mathjax">models</span> (LLMs) to generate contexts around observed strings as a means of facilitating valid frequentist inference. These generated contexts serve to reintroduce uncertainty, incorporate auxiliary information, and facilitate interpr&hellip;
